From e446cc7943f45e546b21ebedc77911523fb38a14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:31:11 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 3/3] sparc64: manage PRIMEPOWER IRQ and firmware
 ownership

Track each physical interrupt map across both Psycho PBMs. Preserve
firmware routes and assign the qualified PCI#01 pin-A source an OS slot
through normal IRQ resource acquisition. Drain pending delivery before
retargeting and retain the assignment across device close and reopen.

Exclude route changes during firmware entry. Closed routes are handed
back and reacquired on return; the qualified root-name query retains an
active route. Other active-device firmware requests are refused. Transfer
the native UART explicitly for orderly monitor and terminal entry, defer
BREAK to process context and require external reset after panic.

Check controller mode and map readback at ownership transitions. An
uncertain transition retains exclusion rather than reusing the slot.
Shared pins remain on a common target; only PCI#01 has CPU1 routing.
Other platforms retain their firmware policy and identity vector mask.

SPARC64 V Supplement F.10.9 Tables F-8/F-10 defines the protected physical
access fault checks. The bridge layout and slot policy are based on
captured firmware and hardware tests; no U2U specification is available.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
